  "lpa_name": "Hounslow",
  "decision_agency": "Borough",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "Reason : 1 - The proposed single-storey rear and side extension and the two-storey side extension, by virtue of their inappropriate size, scale and positioning, would result in an increased sense of enclosure and loss of light on the property at 22 Parkwood Road, which would harm the neighbour's living conditions, contrary to the Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD, and Local Plan Policies CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations), and the principles of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 2 - The proposed single-storey rear and side extension, by virtue of its excessive size and scale, would fail to appear proportionate, subordinate and subservient to the host building. Instead, it would be a bulky and incongruous addition that would harm the character and appearance of the host property and the surrounding area. The proposal is, therefore, contrary to Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture) and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations); Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD, and the principles of the National Planning Policy Framework.",
    "Reason : 3 - The proposed two-storey side extension, by virtue of its excessive size, scale, and inappropriate design and position, would fail to appear subordinate to the host property and the wider area and disrupt the symmetry of the pair of semis. Furthermore, the proposal would lack visual harmony and symmetry due to the discrepancies between the ground and first levels, creating an alien addition to the host property and surrounding area. Therefore, the proposed two-storey side extension would be harmful to the overall character and appearance of the site and surrounding area, contrary to Part A5 of the Hounslow Character, Sustainability and Design Codes SPD and Local Plan Policies CC1 (Context and Character), CC2 (Urban Design and Architecture), and SC7 (Residential Extensions and Alterations)."
  ],
